# JetonBro mandatory Cursor operating rules

Cursor must read this entire file before planning, editing, running commands, or answering any implementation request in this repository.

After every accepted change, Cursor must update this file when the change affects architecture, invariants, state transitions, accounting, permissions, commands, deployment, or the current implementation status.

Cursor must never silently weaken, bypass, delete, or contradict a rule in this file. If a request conflicts with a rule, stop and explain the conflict before editing.

## Product boundary

JetonBro tracks virtual jetons used alongside physical games. Physical cards, physical money, hand evaluation, dealing, randomness, and payment processing are always outside the application.

Blackjack and Texas Hold’em are implemented as separate domain modules. Zilch remains coming later. Poker must never be folded into the Blackjack rules engine.

## Mandatory invariants

1. The server is authoritative for every balance and phase.
2. Every balance mutation creates an immutable ledger entry.
3. Every value-changing command is transactional and idempotent.
4. Ordinary bets and Insurance are separate locked-value accounts.
5. Normal box settlement never settles Insurance.
6. Insurance settlement never settles a normal box.
7. A round cannot complete while any box or Insurance bet remains unresolved.
8. A Player sees only their own boxes and balance.
9. A Player sees all their own open boxes together.
10. The permanent Player bottom area always shows their available value and jetons in every phase.
11. The Bank sees all active boxes.
12. The Bank phase label and transition action remain near the top.
13. Physical cards, real money, dealing, shuffling, suits, decks, and card randomness remain outside the application. Optional rank records may be stored as assistance only; they never replace the physical table and never block play.

## Blackjack phase sequence

`TABLE_SETUP -> BETTING -> PLAYING -> PAYOUT -> ROUND_COMPLETE -> BETTING`

No backward transitions and no phase skipping.

Insurance is a Bank-triggered window during PLAYING, not a phase. It is settled independently during PAYOUT.

## Texas Hold’em phase sequence

`POKER_SETUP -> PRE_FLOP -> FLOP -> TURN -> RIVER -> SHOWDOWN -> HAND_COMPLETE -> PRE_FLOP`

The Table Owner advances physical-card streets only after the current betting round is complete. Blinds post automatically once per hand. If one Player remains, the pot is awarded immediately without Showdown: the current actor and amount to call are cleared, the winner is recorded, and `HAND COMPLETE + TO CALL + WAITING` is impossible. If every remaining Player is All-In, the Owner still deals remaining streets, then Showdown. Next hand rotates the Dealer button once and posts blinds once. Physical cards stay offline; there is no shuffling, dealing, deck, or automatic hand evaluation. Optional community and hole-card records are display-only and never advance a street or settle a pot.

## Texas Hold’em roles and control matrix

These roles stay distinct. The rotating Dealer/Button is never Owner chrome.

- Table Owner (`isOwner`): manages the table and advances physical-card streets.
- Poker Dealer/Button (`seat.isDealer`): rotating playing seat; posts blinds and acts normally; does not receive Owner controls.
- Current Actor: the only Player who may Fold / Check or Call / Bet or Raise / All-In. CALL stays directly available when chips are owed. BET/RAISE opens a local composer; jeton taps and pot drops add to the staged amount and do not move the ledger or the turn until CONFIRM BET / CONFIRM RAISE. Duplicate confirmation is idempotent. The rotating Dealer/Button is never Owner chrome.
- Other Players: see the hand, pot, street, and whose turn it is; cannot act.
- Folded / All-In Players: remain visible with status and the wallet; receive no betting controls or tray.

Lower layout on every playable screen: game-control layer, then a fixed Player wallet (AVAILABLE on the right, shared jeton tray, signed-in Player only, safe-area padding). Owner street controls sit in the game-control layer, visually separated from actor actions. Hide controls the user cannot use; show a disabled street button only to explain that the street is not yet matched. Clients follow snapshot/SSE; `pokerControls()` is the UI acceptance contract.

| Phase | Owner (not acting) | Owner (also actor) | Current actor (not owner) | Other Players | Folded / All-In |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `POKER_SETUP` | DEAL CARDS; SEAT ORDER / + PLAYER / GIVE JETONS / SWITCH GAME in the table menu | — | — | Same felt + wallet | — |
| `PRE_FLOP` | DEAL FLOP visible disabled until matched | DEAL FLOP disabled + actor actions + tray | Actor actions + tray; no DEAL | Same felt; whose turn; wallet; no actions | Seat status + wallet; no actions/tray |
| `FLOP` | DEAL TURN disabled until matched, then enabled | Same + actor set if it is their turn | Same as PRE_FLOP | Same | Same |
| `TURN` | DEAL RIVER disabled until matched, then enabled | Same | Same | Same | Same |
| `RIVER` | SHOWDOWN disabled until matched, then enabled | Same | Same | Same | Same |
| `SHOWDOWN` | ASSIGN WINNERS | No actor actions | No actor actions | Pots/results + wallet | Status + wallet |
| `HAND_COMPLETE` | NEXT HAND NOW, NEXT HAND IN 7 SECONDS; jetons/switch in the table menu | No actor actions | Wallet + result | Wallet + result | Wallet + result |

## Accounting

- Unit: millijetons (`bigint`, 1000 = 1 jeton). Floating-point arithmetic is not used for balances.
- AVAILABLE is `TableMember.availableMillis`.
- LOCKED_BET is `BettingBox.lockedBetMillis`.
- LOCKED_INSURANCE is `InsuranceBet.amountMillis` until Insurance is settled.
- LOCKED_POKER is `PokerParticipant.lockedMillis` until the hand is awarded. Poker wagers move `AVAILABLE → LOCKED_POKER` and never debit or credit `BANK_VIRTUAL_RESERVE`. Side pots follow all-in contribution levels. Split pots divide equally; millijeton remainder is assigned left of the dealer button.
- BANK_VIRTUAL_RESERVE is unlimited and not stored as a balance. In Open Bank it is the source of minted table jetons and payout profit, and the sink of lost ordinary and Insurance stakes.
- Limited Bank stores table-specific `BANK_AVAILABLE` and `BANK_LOCKED_EXPOSURE` in millijetons. Initial funding is `BANK_VIRTUAL_RESERVE → BANK_AVAILABLE` once. Before a Player stake is accepted, the Bank reserves maximum configured box profit exposure (`1.5×` for 3:2, `1.2×` for 6:5). Insurance reserves `2×` Insurance stake independently. Settlement consumes or releases that reserved exposure in the same transaction as the Player ledger. The Player is credited exactly once by the existing `BET_*` / `BLACKJACK_RETURN` / `INSURANCE_*` entry. `BANK_PAYOUT` and `BANK_STAKE_TAKE` are Bank-side legs (`playerId` null), never a second Player credit. Insufficient coverage rejects the Player action without debiting them.
- Commands that change value require an idempotency key and write at least one ledger entry in the same transaction.
- Ordinary payouts: win profit 1× / return 2×; push profit 0 / return 1×; loss return 0; Blackjack 3:2 profit 1.5× / return 2.5×; Blackjack 6:5 profit 1.2× / return 2.2×.
- Insurance 2:1: profit 2× Insurance stake / return 3× Insurance stake. Settled independently of the box.

## Permissions

- Owner: create table, invite, add/remove players before a round, assign Bank/Dealer, distribute jetons, save table, close table and transport remaining AVAILABLE to `PLAYER_POCKET`, or permanently delete an unused empty draft. Dealer reassignment does not transfer ownership.
- Bank/Dealer: open betting, deal cards, Insurance window, payout phase, settle boxes, settle Insurance, start next round. Optionally enter/correct ranks on any Player box and the Dealer hand during PLAYING. During PAYOUT the table owner may use `DEALER WON` to settle every currently unresolved active Player box as `LOST` in one transaction; already-settled boxes stay unchanged and Insurance is never settled by this command. May toggle Open/Limited Bank during unstaked BETTING. The Open/Limited toggle is shown only on the Bank BETTING surface. Players never see it. May change Card Assist during TABLE_SETUP or unstaked BETTING.
- Player: own boxes only; bet/retract during BETTING; Double/Split during PLAYING; Insurance only while the window is open. Optionally enter/correct ranks on their own selected box during PLAYING. Never edit another Player’s box or the Dealer hand. In Texas Hold’em only the current actor may Fold/Check/Call/Bet/Raise/All-in. The rotating Dealer/Button is a seated Player and does not inherit Table Owner street or table-management controls.
- Table Owner: may switch games during TABLE_SETUP, unstaked BETTING, ROUND_COMPLETE, POKER_SETUP, or HAND_COMPLETE. Locked Bet, Insurance, Bank exposure, or LOCKED_POKER blocks switching with `Finish or clear the current hand before switching games`. Switching preserves the table, memberships, AVAILABLE, pockets, owner, invitations/QR, and seat order. Limited Bank buckets freeze in place during Poker and restore unchanged on return to Blackjack.

## Design architecture

- `classic` is the first and default skin.
- Game/domain logic must not import skin components or CSS.
- Skins must not contain permissions, accounting, phase rules, or payout calculations.
- Build shared semantic slots first, then render those slots through the active skin.
- A future skin must be replaceable without changing domain tests.
- Do not create per-skin copies of pages or game logic.

Recommended skin boundary:

```text
src/ui/core/                 semantic screen composition
src/ui/skins/classic/        Classic components, tokens and styles
src/ui/skins/registry.ts     typed skin selection
```

## Deployment

- One Next.js app, one PostgreSQL database.
- In-process SSE is single-instance only. Railway must run exactly one application instance.
- `GET /api/health` reports database connectivity and does not expose secrets.
- `npm run guardrails` before tests and build.
- `npm start` runs `prisma migrate deploy && next start`.
- Railway staging: `preDeployCommand` runs `npx prisma migrate deploy`, then `npx next start`, healthcheck `/api/health`, **exactly one replica**.
- `ALLOW_DEV_MAILBOX` is local/CI only and is ignored when `NODE_ENV=production`. `/api/dev/*` always 404s in production.
- Real email delivery uses the Resend HTTP API (`RESEND_API_KEY` + `EMAIL_FROM`). The API key is never placed in a URL.
- The development mailbox is used only when `NODE_ENV !== "production"` and `ALLOW_DEV_MAILBOX=true`. Production never falls back to it.
- `AUTH_URL` is the public origin for magic links, invitation URLs, and Auth.js redirects. Production redirects must never use `localhost` or `*.railway.internal`.
- Successful magic-link login without an invitation lands on authenticated home (`/`). Invitation callbacks stay on `/join/{token}` using the existing EMAIL/QR token model.
- Creating a table uses domain Blackjack defaults (`THREE_TWO` payout, 3 boxes, Insurance on). The creator is Bank/Dealer and remains in `TABLE_SETUP` until they open betting.
- `CREATE A TABLE` immediately creates or reuses one `TABLE_SETUP` draft and opens `/tables/{tableId}` with a single setup mask over the real Dealer table. The mask shows compact game tiles (Blackjack, Texas Hold’em, Zilch — Coming later), table settings, the complete shared table QR (`SCAN TO JOIN TABLE`, `COPY LINK`, `SHARE`), then compact email invite, with `CREATE TABLE` sticky. There is no separate waiting-room page.
- There is one reusable table QR join URL. Multiple authenticated users may redeem it; each user gets one membership. Email invitations stay individually addressed.
- During `TABLE_SETUP` the Dealer table shows a compact `TABLE SETUP` heading, player boxes for Invited/Joined/Ready, a compact QR overlay control, `+ PLAYER`, and `OPEN BETTING`. The table name is printed only on the cloth. `OPEN BETTING` is enabled only after a Player has joined and is the `TABLE_SETUP -> BETTING` command. Selecting Texas Hold’em on the setup mask and confirming `CREATE TABLE` finalizes the draft as Poker and opens `POKER_SETUP` with no Blackjack round. Poker setup shows the same felt as Players, with Owner-only `DEAL CARDS`. `DEAL CARDS` creates one hand, assigns the rotating Poker Dealer button, posts SB/BB once (`AVAILABLE → LOCKED_POKER`), enters `PRE_FLOP`, and marks the first actor `YOUR TURN`. Switching from Blackjack lands on `POKER_SETUP`; it does not start a hand. Seat order lives in the table menu as compact up/down controls, Owner-only during `POKER_SETUP` before the first `DEAL CARDS`. After that first hand, order is locked (`SEATS_LOCKED`) including `HAND_COMPLETE`. The Dealer button rotates through that stored order. The Table Owner/Host is never the same role as the rotating Poker Dealer/Button (`seat.isDealer`).
- Shared surfaces project the active game with `projectActiveGame`: Blackjack uses the Round phase; Poker uses the PokerHand phase. Home cards, table headers, SSE snapshot ordering, reconnect, save/close eligibility, and owner controls never show a stale Blackjack `Table.currentPhase` while Poker is active. Examples: `Texas Hold’em · PRE-FLOP`, `Texas Hold’em · SHOWDOWN`, `Texas Hold’em · HAND COMPLETE`. Closing or saving a Poker table is blocked while `LOCKED_POKER` exists or an active hand is unsettled.
- Next Poker hand: after `HAND_COMPLETE` the owner uses `NEXT HAND NOW` or `NEXT HAND IN 7 SECONDS`. The seven-second option stores `PokerHand.nextHandDeadlineAt`. Refresh resumes that deadline. At zero, or on `NEXT HAND NOW`, the table rotates the dealer once, posts SB/BB once, and opens exactly one `PRE_FLOP` hand. Duplicate commands cannot create a second hand or post blinds twice.
- The current Poker actor’s seat uses a pulsing gold highlight (`prefers-reduced-motion` uses a static strong outline). Their screen says `YOUR TURN`; other screens say `Waiting for {name}`. Every seat box shows name, AVAILABLE, current-street commitment, status (`YOUR TURN` / Waiting / FOLDED / ALL IN), and D / SB / BB markers. The rotating Poker Dealer box has a D badge and a subtle gold border. The felt is identical for Owner and Players: centre pot is the jeton stack plus total of every committed hand contribution (`settled pots + current street contributions`), `TO CALL {amount}` only when the viewer owes on a live betting street, and main/side-pot lines only when side pots exist. After `HAND_COMPLETE` the pot area shows `POT PAID` and `{name} WON {amount}`; it never keeps `TO CALL`, an actor, or a Waiting seat. `TO CALL` and `CALL {amount}` use the same owed amount; `CALL 0` is never shown. A zero AVAILABLE stack does not receive Call/Bet/Raise and is marked All-In when that player cannot post a blind. Management controls stay out of the felt. Only that actor’s snapshot includes Fold/Check/Call/Bet/Raise/All-In. When chips are owed the actor sees CALL {amount} plus FOLD, RAISE and ALL IN. When nothing is owed they see CHECK, then BET if the street is unopened or RAISE if a wager already exists, plus ALL IN and FOLD. CHECK is never shown while `toCall > 0`. BET/RAISE opens one Classic numeric field; chips add to that field; CONFIRM commits once through `pokerAct`; CALL remains visible while composing a raise. Stale actions return `TURN_CONFLICT` and the client refreshes. Table Owner chrome (`isOwner`) is distinct from the rotating Dealer button (`seat.isDealer`). Owner street buttons `DEAL FLOP` / `DEAL TURN` / `DEAL RIVER` / `SHOWDOWN` sit in the lower game-control layer, compact and visually separated from actor actions, visible disabled with `Waiting for bets to match` until the street is complete, then enabled. Folded and All-In Players keep the wallet and seat status and receive no betting controls. Every playable Player screen uses a fixed bottom wallet (AVAILABLE on the right, shared jeton tray, safe-area padding) with game controls directly above it. The Poker table name appears once on the cloth (`data-table-name`), not in the header. Seat amounts are labelled AVAILABLE and STREET. ALL IN shows the stack. BET opens a street; RAISE uses a Raise-to composer with the legal minimum. A short all-in does not reopen raising for players who already acted. A fold-out awards the complete pot once, including the winner’s own committed blinds.
- During BETTING the Bank may `DEAL CARDS NOW` or `DEAL IN 7 SECONDS`. Both require at least one valid locked player bet (`lockedBetMillis > 0`). Display leftover `originalStakeMillis` does not enable Deal. The seven-second option stores `Round.bettingCloseDeadlineAt` and closes betting exactly once at that deadline. Clients display the same countdown from that deadline. `DEAL CARDS NOW` atomically clears that deadline and enters PLAYING exactly once. A repeated Deal while already PLAYING returns the current snapshot. A Deal sent from the wrong phase returns `PHASE_CONFLICT` and the client refreshes.
- Table stores `startingJetonsPerPlayerMillis`. When an invited user becomes a joined member, that membership is credited once (`starting-jetons:{tableId}:{userId}` plus `TableMember.startingJetonsCredited`). The Bank may later add more with the existing Bank-only control. The Bank is not a betting player.
- Redeem/join retries are idempotent: they do not create a second membership or credit starting jetons twice.
- Betting commands return domain errors (`INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS`, phase/permission messages). A joined Player with starting jetons can lock AVAILABLE into LOCKED_BET during BETTING.
- Live table snapshots use in-process SSE with a short snapshot poll fallback. The listener set is stored on `globalThis` so Next.js module duplication cannot drop updates. Each snapshot includes a server `revision` (`Table.updatedAt` from the database, never client time) and `roundNumber`. Clients and SSE ignore any older in-flight snapshot so a successful Deal cannot be overwritten by a stale BETTING payload. Command failures refresh the snapshot. `Table.currentPhase` is repaired to match `Round.phase` when they diverge. If `currentPhase` is BETTING with no current round, `OPEN BETTING` creates the missing BETTING round. Snapshot and SSE loads skip Blackjack close-betting and next-round timers while `Table.game` is not `BLACKJACK`, including the race immediately after switching to Texas Hold’em. Phase commands log sanitized evidence (table, round, actor, requested transition, phase, round status, bet counts, unresolved counts, deadlines, result code) and never log emails, tokens, join links, or secrets.

## Change discipline

From here, implementation requests use lightweight prompts unless the work falls under the full acceptance process.

Keep the existing architecture, domain rules, ledger, auth, and Classic skin boundaries intact. Implement only the requested change.

### Lightweight prompts (default)

Read this file first.

Implement only the requested change. Keep the existing architecture, domain rules, ledger, auth and Classic skin boundaries intact.

Run only directly affected tests during development. At completion run:

- `npm run guardrails`
- affected Vitest files
- `npm run build`

Do not run the full Playwright suite, generate screenshots, update architecture documents, commit, push or deploy unless explicitly requested.

For visual, copy, or layout changes, affected tests plus build are sufficient until several improvements are batched into one deployment. Make small changes locally, leave them for review, and deploy only when a batch is accepted.

Do not claim completion from code inspection alone.

### Full acceptance process

Use the full acceptance process only for:

- Accounting or ledger changes
- Authentication / invitations
- Phase transitions
- Database migrations
- Releases to Railway

Full acceptance means:

1. Read this file.
2. Read the files and tests directly affected.
3. State the existing invariant or behavior being changed.
4. Keep the change within one vertical slice.
5. Run focused tests during development.
6. Run guardrails, the full Vitest suite, production build, and the Playwright coverage that proves the changed flow.
7. Render affected 390x844 mobile states and verify at 320x700 when the UI is part of the change.
8. Update this file and `CHANGELOG.md` when architectural facts, invariants, permissions, commands, deployment, or status changed.
9. Commit, push, and deploy only when explicitly requested.
10. Report exact results and genuine limitations.

## Current status

- Repository: Blackjack MVP and Texas Hold’em MVP with authenticated welcome / create-table journey
- Current game: Blackjack MVP and Texas Hold’em MVP
- Next milestone: Zilch remains coming later
- Current skin: Classic
- Accepted references: `design/reference/classic/`
- Bank accounting: Open Bank uses unlimited `BANK_VIRTUAL_RESERVE`. Limited Bank stores table-specific `BANK_AVAILABLE` and `BANK_LOCKED_EXPOSURE` in millijetons. Poker locks `LOCKED_POKER` from Player AVAILABLE and never touches Bank buckets. Card Assist defaults to `OFF`. Optional rank records and Limited Bank accounting are accepted: Player credited once per settlement; `BANK_PAYOUT` / `BANK_STAKE_TAKE` are Bank-side; table value `AVAILABLE + LOCKED_BET + LOCKED_INSURANCE + LOCKED_POKER + BANK_AVAILABLE + BANK_LOCKED_EXPOSURE` is conserved except explicit `BANK_VIRTUAL_RESERVE` funding. Limited Bank buckets freeze in place while Texas Hold’em is active.
- Table settings: `blackjackPayout`, `maxBoxesPerPlayer` (default 3), `insuranceEnabled` (default true), and `startingJetonsPerPlayerMillis` are server-authoritative
- Starting jetons: credited once on join to the player membership, never to the Bank as a betting stack. The Poker table owner is a seated Player and receives the starting allocation.
- Authenticated home: compact open-table rows show table name, game, phase, Bank/Dealer name, current Players, player/box counts, and `RETURN TO TABLE`. While Poker is active the row shows the projected Hold’em headline, never a leftover Blackjack round phase. The owner sees every Player’s table balance; a non-owner sees Player names and only their own balance. The owner overflow shows `DELETE TABLE` on an empty draft, or `SAVE TABLE` and `CLOSE TABLE & SAVE BALANCES` on a started table. It does not also offer `CLOSE & REMOVE TABLE`.
- Dealer `TABLE_SETUP`: after `CREATE TABLE`, the real table surface is visible immediately. Compact QR overlay and `+ PLAYER` stay in the top controls. No permanent centre QR / waiting-room page. `CREATE TABLE` finalizes the existing draft; it does not add a second setup step.
- Betting close: `Round.bettingCloseDeadlineAt` is the server-authoritative 7-second deal deadline
- Next round: after every box and required Insurance stake is settled, the Bank uses `NEXT ROUND NOW` or `IN 7 SECONDS`. The seven-second option stores `Round.nextRoundDeadlineAt` (not `bettingCloseDeadlineAt`). Refresh resumes that deadline. At zero, or on `NEXT ROUND NOW`, the table opens exactly one new BETTING round. A PAYOUT snapshot that already has every required settlement settled can enable next-round. A blocked restart returns `NEXT_ROUND_BLOCKED`.
- Dealer PAYOUT: compact vertical player list. Each box has its own horizontal result rail, left to right: `LOST`, `STAND OFF` (PUSH), `BLACKJACK`, `WON`. Gestures bind to the complete unresolved payout row with Pointer Events and `setPointerCapture`: swipe left LOST, swipe right WON, double-tap STAND OFF/PUSH; BLACKJACK is button-only. Outcome buttons stop propagation and do not start a swipe. Gestures settle only that box. Labels come from `suggestedPayout`. Insurance is independent of box swipes. Owner-only `DEALER WON` is a bulk convenience that runs the existing per-box `LOST` ledger rules for every currently unresolved active box in one transaction; it is idempotent and never settles Insurance.
- Classic Blackjack table: one app/phone frame only. The green felt is the table. There is no nested wood/leather rail. Every live Dealer phase (BETTING, PLAYING, PAYOUT, ROUND_COMPLETE) uses the same compact `DealerBlackjackBoxRow`. The DEALER hand is that same compact row at the top of the list. Optional `+ CARDS` and entered ranks stay inline in the row during PLAYING and do not expand into a large card panel. Physical cards remain authoritative. The live `Table.name` is printed once on the Blackjack cloth (`data-table-name`). Above the cloth the Bank and Player screens use a compact phase heading and essential phase controls only. A Player with two or more boxes swipes the box cluster left/right to change the selected box; taps and vertical movement do not navigate, and box actions always target the selected box.
- Player celebrations use the settlement ID/box state as the dedupe key: Blackjack always plays the strong overlay once after confirmed settlement; a win sometimes plays the strong overlay and otherwise stays on the row; push is a calm return; loss is restrained Tough Luck. The Dealer keeps compact row confirmation only. Reduced motion disables overlays. Polling, SSE duplication, and refresh must not replay them.
- Owner SAVE TABLE sets `Table.pausedAt` and keeps membership, table balances, Card Assist, funding mode, Limited Bank buckets, optional rank records, and ledger history. `CLOSE TABLE & SAVE BALANCES` is owner-only. Empty drafts (`TABLE_SETUP`, no joined Players, no ledger, no staked rounds) may be hard-deleted with unused invitations/tokens (`DELETE TABLE`). A started table is never hard-deleted: `CLOSE TABLE & SAVE BALANCES` requires `ROUND_COMPLETE` or `TABLE_SETUP` with no locked Bet/Insurance and no Bank exposure, or Poker `POKER_SETUP` / `HAND_COMPLETE` with no `LOCKED_POKER` and no unsettled hand. It transfers Player AVAILABLE to `PLAYER_POCKET` exactly once via the existing close-table transaction (`TABLE_TRANSFER_OUT`), archives the table including remaining Limited Bank history, removes it from Open Tables, and keeps ledger/round/card history. Locked funds, Bank exposure, or an active Poker hand return `LOCKED_FUNDS`. Later joins write `TABLE_TRANSFER_IN`. Open Bank virtual reserve is not stored or transported into a Player pocket. Dealer reassignment does not transfer ownership.
- Player is credited exactly once per settlement by the existing `BET_*` / `BLACKJACK_RETURN` / `INSURANCE_*` ledger row. `BANK_PAYOUT` and `BANK_STAKE_TAKE` are Bank-side legs (`playerId` null) in the same transaction.
- Verification: lightweight local changes use guardrails, affected Vitest, and `next build`. Full Playwright, screenshots, commit, push, and Railway deploy only for ledger/auth/phase/migration work or an accepted release batch
- Staging target: one Railway app replica, one PostgreSQL service, health `/api/health`, `ALLOW_DEV_MAILBOX=false`
- Email delivery: Resend HTTP API. Magic-link sign-in works on production
- Phase commands: `OPEN BETTING` starts Betting; `DEAL CARDS NOW` closes Betting and starts Playing; `PAYOUT PHASE` moves Playing to Payout; `NEXT ROUND NOW` starts the next Betting round. Wrong-phase clicks return `PHASE_CONFLICT` or `NEXT_ROUND_BLOCKED` instead of a silent no-op
- Texas Hold’em role × phase control matrix is the accepted UI contract (`pokerControls()`). Owner chrome follows `isOwner`; the Dealer button is `seat.isDealer` only. `DEAL CARDS` starts a hand from `POKER_SETUP`. Seat order is menu-only and locks after the first hand. CALL remains available while BET/RAISE is composed; chips stage until confirm. Shared bottom wallet and game-control layers apply to Blackjack and Poker. Snapshot/SSE loads skip Blackjack close-betting while Poker is active.
- `DEAL FLOP` / `DEAL TURN` / `DEAL RIVER` each call `startBettingStreet`: reset only street contribution / `hasActedThisStreet` / street wager, preserve totals and `LOCKED_POKER`, assign the first active non-folded non-All-In Player left of the rotating D (`postflopFirstPlayerId`), increment `PokerHand.actionCount`, and bump `Table.updatedAt` so snapshot/SSE show the new street and actor immediately. Owner `SHOWDOWN` stays disabled until River betting is matched. If every remaining Player is All-In, the Owner runs streets with a null actor.
- A fold-out or showdown payout marks `HAND_COMPLETE` with `currentActorPlayerId = null`, `streetWagerMillis = 0`, and `toCall = 0` on every snapshot. The felt shows `POT PAID` plus `{name} WON {amount}`. Seats never stay Waiting after the hand ends.
- Compact street rail `DEAL → PRE-FLOP → FLOP → TURN → RIVER → SHOWDOWN` is shared by Owner and Players (`pokerStreetRail()`). Current is gold; completed are subtle; future are muted.
- Optional physical-card assist: Owner may enter community cards (flop exactly 3, then +1 turn, +1 river). Each Player may enter their own 2 hole cards. Community values are public; hole values are viewer-only (`hasHoleCards` for everyone else). The table screen stays collapsed (`+ HOLE CARDS` / `+ BOARD CARDS`); rank/suit entry is a temporary sheet that closes on SAVE or CANCEL. Card commands do not advance phase, settle pots, or write ledger rows, and idempotency hashes `tableId` only so values are not logged. Manual Showdown remains authoritative; there is no automatic hand evaluation.
- `CREATE NEW TABLE` / `CREATE A TABLE` navigate to `/tables/new`, which `ensureDraftTable`s one draft and redirects to `/tables/{id}`. Repeated clicks reuse that draft. After finalize, the same table route uses the setup felt plus the black bottom dock (`QR`, `+ PLAYER`, `OPEN BETTING`); Card Assist and Bank funding stay in the compact table menu.
- Classic visual system: deep emerald felt with a CSS texture, antique-gold details, cream serif headings, matte-black `--dock`, and CSS-rendered jetons. Blackjack and Poker print `Table.name` once on the cloth (`data-table-name`) and never again in the header. Blackjack uses a single phone/felt frame with compact stacked Dealer box rows in every live phase and no nested wood/leather table shell. Poker uses a compact shared felt without the large oval or decorative gold dots. Optional cards, street rail (`PRE-FLOP · FLOP · TURN · RIVER · SHOWDOWN` on active hands), and command availability are unchanged except owner-only `DEALER WON` during PAYOUT. Implemented locally; uncommitted and undeployed.
- Next milestone: Zilch remains coming later
